1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,310
Welcome to Lesson 3.1: Locating the Patient Profile.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,118
When you receive a patient task,

3
00:00:11,168 --> 00:00:17,281
the first thing to do is to locate the patient in the three systems you'll use along the process.

4
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:20,286
First, pull your task from the task portal.

5
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:23,229
Then find the patient in PointClickCare.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,930
In ThoroughCare.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,946
And in Practice Fusion.

8
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,633
Every case starts with a patient task.

9
00:00:30,683 --> 00:00:34,917
To see which patients are assigned to you, use the task portal.

10
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,263
From the task portal,

11
00:00:36,313 --> 00:00:40,263
you can pull the patient tasks that are currently assigned to you.

12
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:46,259
Enter the agent code assigned to you, in this box.

13
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,332
Then click Pull Task.

14
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,202
The task loads, and the patient's information appears.

15
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,304
It shows the facility where the patient lives,

16
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:58,451
the patient's date of birth,

17
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:00,450
the patient's full name,

18
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,493
and the patient's primary provider.

19
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:08,899
The last service date shows when the patient was last followed up.

20
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:13,454
ICD-10 is the code of the condition you'll follow up on.

21
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:17,844
And the task type is either follow-up, or scratch.

22
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,086
Below them are two dropdowns.

23
00:01:20,136 --> 00:01:23,694
Once you complete the case, you'll use them to submit it,

24
00:01:23,744 --> 00:01:25,839
as completed or otherwise.

25
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,871
So now you have the task, and the patient's information.

26
00:01:30,133 --> 00:01:34,832
The first thing to do next is to find out how you'll access the patient's chart,

27
00:01:34,882 --> 00:01:36,401
in PointClickCare.

28
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:38,914
Because of HIPAA guidelines,

29
00:01:38,964 --> 00:01:43,113
logging in to PointClickCare asks for an authentication code.

30
00:01:43,367 --> 00:01:47,861
But before that, you need to know which username and password to log in with,

31
00:01:47,911 --> 00:01:50,190
to find this patient's profile.

32
00:01:50,467 --> 00:01:53,971
Our patients live in skilled nursing facilities, or SNFs.

33
00:01:54,021 --> 00:01:56,155
There are hundreds of them.

34
00:01:56,433 --> 00:01:59,657
Groups of these facilities, say 20, 30, or 50,

35
00:01:59,707 --> 00:02:02,932
have their own credentials: their own username

36
00:02:02,982 --> 00:02:07,133
and password to open their charts in PointClickCare.

37
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:11,983
To find them, take the facility from the patient's task,

38
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:17,477
and search for it, by name, in the sheet we call PCC Map.

39
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:22,525
The facility's row shows the username and the password to log in with.

40
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:25,845
Copy them,

41
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:30,192
and log in to PointClickCare with this username and password.

42
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:35,060
Paste the username, and click Next.

43
00:02:38,733 --> 00:02:41,175
PointClickCare asks for the password.

44
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,220
Paste it, and sign in.

45
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,620
The first time you log in with a set of credentials,

46
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:50,985
PointClickCare asks for an authentication code.

47
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:57,026
To get it, ask your direct manager, your SME, your DTL, or your team leader.

48
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:04,496
Here, the code comes from the authenticator.

49
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,610
Enter the code in these boxes.

50
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:16,917
Tick Remember this device for 30 days, so the code is remembered on this device.

51
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,281
Then you won't need to enter it again,

52
00:03:19,331 --> 00:03:22,416
each time you log in with the same credentials.

53
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:24,119
Now, verify.

54
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:26,740
You're in PointClickCare.

55
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:29,448
Now, locate the patient's profile.

56
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:34,063
From the task, take the patient's name.

57
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:38,217
In PointClickCare, you can search for a patient by first name,

58
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:41,065
last name, or social security number.

59
00:03:42,367 --> 00:03:45,508
You also know which facility the patient is in.

60
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:50,991
Each set of credentials opens the charts of several facilities, not just one.

61
00:03:51,267 --> 00:03:53,688
So first, switch to the patient's facility.

62
00:03:53,738 --> 00:03:55,796
Then search for the patient.

63
00:03:56,067 --> 00:03:58,879
Click the facility name, at the top right.

64
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:04,285
The list shows every facility these credentials can open.

65
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,206
Search for the patient's facility by name.

66
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,212
Here it is.

67
00:04:20,262 --> 00:04:21,406
Select it.

68
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:24,265
The facility now shows at the top right.

69
00:04:24,315 --> 00:04:26,347
You're in the right facility.

70
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:32,477
Now, use the search box at the top to find the resident by name.

71
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:35,312
Enter the patient's name, and search.

72
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,716
And here's the patient's profile.

73
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:47,869
Sometimes, the search finds nothing.

74
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:51,061
That's because it searches current residents only.

75
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:54,864
If the patient is discharged, deceased, on the waiting list,

76
00:04:54,914 --> 00:04:57,929
or anything else, the profile won't appear.

77
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:04,048
In that case, switch the search to all residents,

78
00:05:05,867 --> 00:05:09,639
and search for the patient again, until you find the profile.

79
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,242
That's the first step.

80
00:05:11,292 --> 00:05:14,971
The patient's profile in PointClickCare is located.

81
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:18,858
Next, do the same in ThoroughCare, and Practice Fusion.

82
00:05:20,867 --> 00:05:22,519
Next, ThoroughCare.

83
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:27,443
For a follow-up task, the patient already has a profile in ThoroughCare.

84
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:30,900
But a scratch patient has no profile in ThoroughCare yet,

85
00:05:30,950 --> 00:05:32,939
so you'll create a new one.

86
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:44,388
Here, the task type is follow-up, so the profile already exists.

87
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:48,999
You can search ThoroughCare by date of birth, or by first or last name.

88
00:05:49,049 --> 00:05:50,980
Search by date of birth.

89
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:53,986
Use the search box at the top left.

90
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:56,844
Enter the date of birth, and press Enter.

91
00:05:58,967 --> 00:06:02,439
The worklist shows every patient with that date of birth.

92
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:06,939
Find your patient, and open the profile.

93
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:11,606
The patient's profile in ThoroughCare is located.

94
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:17,132
Last, locate the same patient in Practice Fusion.

95
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:20,378
Log in with your own username and password.

96
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:32,387
Practice Fusion is divided into tabs, on the left: Home,

97
00:06:32,437 --> 00:06:36,218
Schedule, Tasks, Charts, Messages, and Reports.

98
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,789
To search for a patient's profile, open Charts.

99
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,299
A search box opens.

100
00:06:41,349 --> 00:06:43,798
You can search by name, date of birth,

101
00:06:43,848 --> 00:06:47,850
or the last four digits of the social security number.

102
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,926
Search by date of birth.

103
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,468
It avoids opening another patient who has the same name,

104
00:06:53,518 --> 00:06:56,991
but a different date of birth: a different patient.

105
00:06:57,467 --> 00:06:59,232
Enter the date of birth.

106
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:03,870
The results show the patient profiles with that date of birth.

107
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:08,185
Find your patient, and click the profile.

108
00:07:08,467 --> 00:07:11,695
This is the patient's profile in Practice Fusion.

109
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:16,833
Now you've matched the patient's profile in all three systems: PointClickCare,

110
00:07:16,883 --> 00:07:19,389
ThoroughCare, and Practice Fusion.

111
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:22,392
To recap.

112
00:07:22,667 --> 00:07:24,988
Pull your task with your agent code.

113
00:07:25,267 --> 00:07:29,765
Find the facility's username and password in the PCC Map.

114
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:35,321
The first time, ask for the authentication code, and tick Remember this device.

115
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:40,110
In PointClickCare, switch to the patient's facility, then search by name.

116
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:43,234
If nothing comes up, search all residents.

117
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:46,046
In ThoroughCare, search by date of birth.

118
00:07:46,096 --> 00:07:48,952
A scratch patient needs a new profile.

119
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:53,540
And in Practice Fusion, open Charts, and search by date of birth.

120
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,551
That's the end of Lesson 3.1.

121
00:07:58,833 --> 00:08:02,595
Next, in Lesson 3.2: eligibility checks.
